    <span class="notice">
      <br>
      Note that this data center is no longer updated.
      <br><br><br>
    </span>


  @(ssr-right-content
    <div id='datacenter_right_col'>
      <b>$(title)</b>
      <br><br>
      <div style="height:$(column-height); overflow: auto">
        An SSR, or "Single Sequence Repeat", also called a "microsatellite",
        is a DNA pattern of 1 - 10 nucleotides that are repeated in tandem. 
        SSRs are commonly used as genetic markers.
        <br><br>
        For more information about SSRs and how they are used, see 
        <a href="https://dx.doi.org/10.1590%2F1678-4685-GMB-2016-0027">Vierira et al., 2016</a>.
      </div>
	  </div>
  )
)

